From 8a97e559bbdae0a256a9d953d5535f133bd323d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:03:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 74/75] grate: layout v2: a value is the same in either half of
 a register

The evaluator hashed sub_reg_select_high into every source operand, so
the same value read from the low half in the sequential program and
from the high half after layout looked different, and layout v2
rejected the result ("the signature differs"). That happens whenever
the common subexpression elimination of interpolations lets the
allocator keep a copy in the high half: color_rounded_gray was rejected
and fell back to the old layout (72 steps, 96 packets).

For FIXED10 reads of a register or a forward the leaf already is the
value of the selected half, so which half is read is a choice of
location. lo_src no longer mixes the half-select bit in for those.

Checked on the tablet with a rounded rectangle (1000x500, radius 80)
through the same shader: color_rounded_gray is now 15 steps and 25
packets (NVIDIA 24 and 32) instead of 72 and 96, and 4.4 times faster
(55 ms against 242 ms for a full-screen quad). Its pixels match a CPU
model to within 1/255 on all 1366x768 pixels; the installed library and
GRATE_LAYOUT_V1=1 are wrong on about 5700 pixels in the rounded
corners. The other shape shaders (color, color_rounded, border,
premult_rounded, glyph) give the same pixels as before, and the
tools/gpu self-checking tests behave as before.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/layout.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/layout.c b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/layout.c
index 81682887e95..ec7d4e07fc8 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/layout.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/layout.c
@@ -246,9 +246,19 @@ lo_src(const struct lo_eval *e, const struct fp_alu_src_operand *s, int64_t q,
        int round)
 {
    uint64_t leaf = lo_leaf(e, s, q, round);
-   uint64_t a[] = {
-      leaf,         s->negate,   s->absolute_value,     s->scale_by_two,
-      s->minus_one, s->datatype, s->sub_reg_select_high};
+   /* Which half of a register or forward a half-precision operand reads is a
+    * choice of location: the leaf already is the value of that half, and a
+    * value stored in a half is the same whichever half holds it. */
+   const bool half_select =
+      s->datatype == FP_DATATYPE_FIXED10 &&
+      (lo_reg_ok(s->index) || (s->index >= 24 && s->index <= 27));
+   uint64_t a[] = {leaf,
+                   s->negate,
+                   s->absolute_value,
+                   s->scale_by_two,
+                   s->minus_one,
+                   s->datatype,
+                   half_select ? 0 : s->sub_reg_select_high};
    return mixn(7, a);
 }
 
